RISC3D test kit 32 (prototype, 15 November 2026)
================================================

Kit 31's results: rol-3d 0.18's fix mended lit parts 1-5, but not
part 6 (normal not in an array), and not TORCS. TORCS's main drawing
is lit and textured with normal, texture and vertex arrays (part 2's
case, now fixed) but it also has fog on, which the lit test didn't.

This kit checks fog and the lone normal:

 - litx2 draws twelve more lit variations with Linux's Mesa directly,
   each with 0.18's fix applied: fog of several kinds, the normal not
   in an array, a colour array, and two that should be wrong or right
   for comparison.
 - replay redraws your TORCS recording with 0.18's fix, as normal and
   without fog.

Nothing to install (keep riscos-risc3d 0.18-1).

Steps
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing kit 31.
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/litx2
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/replay /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-477.r3d 240

